ical expertise."}]]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-8","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[28px] font-medium leading-8 text-foreground/80","children":"Discovery process"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4","children":[["$","li","Method",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Method"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Double Diamond. Rapid prototyping. Quantitative and qualitative research."}]]}],["$","li","Interviews",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Interviews"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Conducted interviews with 12 frequent users to uncover frustrations and preferences."}]]}],["$","li","Behavioral data",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Behavioral data"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Analyzed behavioral data to identify bottlenecks in the current flow."}]]}],["$","li","Competitors",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Competitors"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Researched competitors to identify best practices."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","figure","2",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-3","children":["$L4b",null]}],"$L4c","$L4d","$L4e","$L4f"]}]]}]
38:["$","section","designs",{"id":"designs","aria-labelledby":"designs-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] border-x border-foreground/5","children":[["$","div",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"pointer-events-none relative h-px","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute -inset-x-[129px] top-0 h-px bg-foreground/5"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-0 grid size-5 -translate-y-1/2 place-items-center rounded-full bg-background left-0 -translate-x-1/2","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"size-0.5 rounded-full bg-foreground"}]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-0 grid size-5 -translate-y-1/2 place-items-center rounded-full bg-background right-0 translate-x-1/2","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"size-0.5 rounded-full bg-foreground"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-6 pb-10 pt-24 md:px-12 lg:pt-40","children":["$","h2",null,{"id":"designs-title","className":"text-2xl font-medium leading-8 md:text-[32px] md:leading-[42px]","children":"Designs and Prototyping"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] border-x border-foreground/5 flex flex-col gap-12 px-6 pb-24 pt-12 md:px-[41px]","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":[null,null,[["$","p","We came to ideation and validation of two major features to follow one another. First was HITL and second was post-processing.",{"className":"text-lg leading-[27px] text-foreground/80","children":"We came to ideation and validation of two major features to follow one another. First was HITL and second was post-processing."}],["$","p","I rapid-prototyped findings in Figma and put clickable versions in front of users across several rounds, testing with real documents rather than sample data. Early rounds showed the confidence indicators worked but the label setup table didn't, users couldn't tell which fields were required or how nesting behaved so we reworked the hierarchy affordances and added inline instructions. Later rounds validated the core loop: participants could review, correct, and approve output on their own, and the corrections they made fed back as training signal, which was the point.",{"className":"text-lg leading-[27px] text-foreground/80","children":"I rapid-prototyped findings in Figma and put clickable versions in front of users across several rounds, testing with real documents rather than sample data. Early rounds showed the confidence indicators worked but the label setup table didn't, users couldn't tell which fields were required or how nesting behaved so we reworked the hierarchy affordances and added inline instructions. Later rounds validated the core loop: participants could review, correct, and approve output on their own, and the corrections they made fed back as training signal, which was the point."}],["$","p","Design centered on one screen: the document on the left, the model's extracted output on the right, so every value could be checked against its source without leaving the page. Confidence scores sit next to each field and drive a color-coded scale, turning review from a full read-through into a triage — low-confidence fields pull attention first, everything else can be skimmed. A pending/completed queue tracks progress across long batches, and the label configuration moved into a plain table where users define fields, parents, data types, formats, and whether a value repeats — enough structure to support line items and nested hierarchies without exposing anything model-shaped. Alongside the happy path, we prototyped the failure states: what a flagged error looks like, who it gets assigned to, and how it's communicated back to the user.",{"className":"text-lg leading-[27px] text-foreground/80","children":"Design centered on one screen: the document on the left, the model's extracted output on the right, so every value could be checked against its source without leaving the page. Confidence scores sit next to each field and drive a color-coded scale, turning review from a full read-through into a triage — low-confidence fields pull attention first, everything else can be skimmed. A pending/completed queue tracks progress across long batches, and the label configuration moved into a plain table where users define fields, parents, data types, formats, and whether a value repeats — enough structure to support line items and nested hierarchies without exposing anything model-shaped. Alongside the happy path, we prototyped the failure states: what a flagged error looks like, who it gets assigned to, and how it's communicated back to the user."}]]]}],"$L50","$L51","$L52"]}]]}]
39:["$","section","lessons",{"id":"lessons","aria-labelledby":"lessons-title","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] border-x border-foreground/5","children":[["$","div",null,{"aria-hidden":true,"className":"pointer-events-none relative h-px","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute -inset-x-[129px] top-0 h-px bg-foreground/5"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-0 grid size-5 -translate-y-1/2 place-items-center rounded-full bg-background left-0 -translate-x-1/2","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"size-0.5 rounded-full bg-foreground"}]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"absolute top-0 grid size-5 -translate-y-1/2 place-items-center rounded-full bg-background right-0 translate-x-1/2","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"size-0.5 rounded-full bg-foreground"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-6 pb-10 pt-24 md:px-12 lg:pt-40","children":["$","h2",null,{"id":"lessons-title","className":"text-2xl font-medium leading-8 md:text-[32px] md:leading-[42px]","children":"Impact and Lessons"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto w-full max-w-[1200px] border-x border-foreground/5 flex flex-col gap-12 px-6 pb-24 pt-12 md:px-[41px]","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[28px] font-medium leading-8 text-foreground/80","children":"Impact"}],null,[["$","p","HITL shipped as the trust layer on top of DeepOpinion's document processing — and trust turned out to be the thing standing between the product and adoption. Users in high-consequence settings stopped treating model output as something to accept or redo wholesale, and started treating it as a draft they could verify in seconds.",{"className":"text-lg leading-[27px] text-foreground/80","children":"HITL shipped as the trust layer on top of DeepOpinion's document processing — and trust turned out to be the thing standing between the product and adoption. Users in high-consequence settings stopped treating model output as something to accept or redo wholesale, and started treating it as a draft they could verify in seconds."}]]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-8","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-[28px] font-medium leading-8 text-foreground/80","children":"What made the difference"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3","children":[["$","li","Visual confidence scoring",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Visual confidence scoring"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Review effort goes where the model is uncertain, not everywhere."}]]}],["$","li","Split-screen validation",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Split-screen validation"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"Extracted data sits beside the source document, so verification is a glance rather than a hunt."}]]}],["$","li","Hierarchical labeling and line-item validation",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-muted-foreground","children":"Hierarchical labeling and line-item validation"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm","children":"The structure finally matches how invoices and contracts actually work, down to nested line properties."}]]}],["$","li","Dynamic label editing",{"className":"rounded-[24px] border border-border/50 bg-secondary flex flex-col gap-2 px-[25px] py-[39px] leading-[22px]","children":["$L53","$L54"]}],"$L55"]}]]}],"$L56","$L57"]}]]}]
